{
  "$comment": [
    "Scene-to-scene flow of Petronius, reconstructed by hand (the original APK decided it at runtime via GPS / voice / QR).",
    "Hand-curated: NOT generated by tools/extract-scenes.mjs. Beat ids refer to data/story/scenes/<scene>.json.",
    "exits[].requires = scenes that must have been played first (where the keyword / clue is learned); 'hub' exits return to the hub scene's list of spokes.",
    "places[].radius = arrival distance in metres for on-site mode (default 60; larger for the campus, long streets and approximate spots).",
    "exits[].after = a scene that plays first (e.g. the QR at the university door on the night return), then this exit applies the next day.",
    "exits[].from = the scene's last beat on that path (the one before `loading`, a `waitsFor` beat, or a video/ending).",
    "exits[].via: gps | voice | qr | ending. `where` is the place the player must reach; `say` is the voice keyword.",
    "confidence: confirmed (APK trigger + explicit text) | likely (explicit address or strong textual link) | guess.",
    "Voice scenes are visited with or without the keyword: knowing it jumps to the sibling scene, otherwise the",
    "'don't remember' branch continues the walk. The same place can therefore be visited twice (e.g. 22-1).",
    "exits[].told = what the player was told that leads here, shown on the next-place card and in the notebook: { beat, match? } = a line of the exit's own scene (the sentence containing `match`, else the whole line); { note: '<scene>#<beat>' } = the note of that solved clue; on voice exits { scene, beat, match } = the line elsewhere that teaches the word, recorded in the notebook when it is read."
  ],
